 "decisions": [
  {
   "title": "Data of the VSAM files moves to relational tables",
   "context": "ORDENES and CUENTAS are VSAM KSDS files read and rewritten with CICS commands. PAGOMOV is not in the inputs.",
   "decision": "ORDENES and CUENTAS become the tables orders and accounts of the target database (data_strategy migration). The legacy precision is kept: S9(9)V99 becomes decimal(11,2), S9(11)V99 becomes decimal(13,2), S9(3)V99 becomes decimal(5,2). Status values P (pending) and G (paid) of orders and A/I of accounts are kept as they are.",
   "consequences": "A data migration is needed before go-live. Reads for update become row locks inside the transaction."
  },
  {
   "title": "The LINK to PAGODEB is absorbed into the PayOrder use case",
   "context": "PAGOORD debits the account with EXEC CICS LINK to PAGODEB (rules 001 to 005). PAGODEB is only called from PAGOORD, passes data through a commarea and has no entry point of its own in the traces.",
   "decision": "The debit logic is implemented inside PayOrder using AccountRepository, in the legacy order: account not found, type mismatch, inactive, balance lower than the total, then the balance is reduced. The PAGODEB response codes are mapped as in PAGOORD: 10 gives CUENTA INACTIVA, 20 gives SALDO INSUFICIENTE, and 30 and 40 give CUENTA NO VALIDA. The debit is not exposed as a separate endpoint.",
   "consequences": "The debit and the order update commit or roll back together, which is stricter than the legacy (two programs under one syncpoint). The PAGODEB commarea disappears."
  },
  {
   "title": "Transaction boundary of the payment",
   "context": "PAGOORD works inside one logical unit of work, which ends with the SYNCPOINT after the order is rewritten. It has no savepoints and no explicit rollback points. Rejections happen before anything is written.",
   "decision": "PayOrder is transactional from begin (line 37) to commit (line 172). Business rejections raise the error before any write, so no rollback entry is needed. Any technical exception rolls back the whole unit.",
   "consequences": "A rejection never leaves partial changes: balance and order stay untouched, as the traces show. No UnitOfWork port is needed because there are no savepoints."
  },
  {
   "title": "PAGOMOV is an external program behind a port",
   "context": "PAGOMOV is not in the inputs and is stubbed in the traces. It receives the order number (MOV_ORDEN) and returns the movement number (MOV_NUMERO).",
   "decision": "It is accessed through the MovementGateway port, with a generated adapter for PAGOMOV. The legacy ignores the status of the LINK, and the design keeps that behaviour.",
   "consequences": "The real PAGOMOV must be provided or migrated in a later step. Tests use the stub of the traces."
  },
  {
   "title": "Screens and pseudo-conversation are replaced by REST",
   "context": "The legacy uses BMS maps (PAGOMEN, PAGOORD, PAGORES), the PGMN and PGOR transactions, a 13-byte commarea, PF keys and XCTL between programs.",
   "decision": "Each use case is a REST endpoint. The commarea, the map handling, PF3 and the key validation (TECLA NO VALIDA) are not translated. The menu routes the option and returns the destination. Rejection messages go in the error response with the same text as the legacy message. CA-ULTIMA-ORDEN lived only in the pseudo-conversational session and is not persisted.",
   "consequences": "Navigation is the responsibility of the client. The text of the messages is kept so the golden master can compare it."
  },
  {
   "title": "The entered amount arrives as a decimal",
   "context": "The map field VALOR is PIC 9(9)V99 and the legacy computes NUMVAL(VALORI)/100 before comparing it with ORD-VALOR. The traces enter 1500.00 for an order of 1500.00 and the payment succeeds.",
   "decision": "The amount is a decimal(11,2) input. The comparison with the order value (RULE-012) is made exactly, with no rounding. The scaling of the screen text is the job of the entry adapter.",
   "consequences": "The business comparison is the same as the traces show. The scaling of the raw screen input has to be confirmed by a reviewer."
  },
  {
   "title": "Text inputs keep their validation",
   "context": "Order number, company and account arrive as text, and RULE-007 requires a numeric and non-zero order number.",
   "decision": "PayOrder receives them as text(fixed) and validates them as in the legacy before converting them to numbers for the repositories. Validations run in the legacy order: order number, account type, channel, approval key. Only the first error is reported.",
   "consequences": "An order number such as 12A4567 is rejected with INVALID_ORDER_NUMBER, never with a type error."
  }
 ],
